WEBVTT

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.500
Today, the final results of
the exam will be announced.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.530
A short while after that, together with
the names of the successful candidates,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.870
the winners of the gold medal of honor
and the Avery scholarship

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.150
will be put up on the bulletin board.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:57.060
Jane is sure she will pass, and having
set her mind on a new goal,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.460
she's not worried at all.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.400
She's happy.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.900
But it's different for Anne.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.290
Although ambitions are well worth having,

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.670
they are not to be cheaply won,

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.400
but exact their dues of work,

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:21.490
self-denial, anxiety and disappointment.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.150
What's wrong, Anne?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.020
Oh, Jane, I'm so worried that I think
my heart will stop beating.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.060
What are you saying, Anne?

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:36.230
You'll win either the gold medal
or the Avery scholarship.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.860
No. I've no hope for the Avery scholarship.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.400
Everybody says Emily Clay will win it.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.900
That's just a rumour started by Josie.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:49.740
She likes to spread such ungrounded rumors.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.650
But this time I feel the same way, too.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:03.720
Don't worry, Anne. You've worked harder
than all of us over the past year.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.400
Your hard work will be rewarded.
Hasn't it been so up until now?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.910
Yes. You'll definitely come in first, Anne.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.120
It will be all right! You will
win one or the other of them.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.570
I'm certain of it.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.080
Now, stop worrying. Let's go.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:22.640
Yes.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.160
Matthew. How come you're
still here at this hour?

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.060
Nothing, I...

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.160
The results will be announced this morning.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.170
Yes.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.810
Anne will win the Avery scholarship,
don't you think?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.500
If she doesn't, she'll be very disappointed.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.770
She has worked so hard
with that as a goal.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:07.550
Yes, Marilla. Don't worry.
There's no one who can match her.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.000
No, I don't have the courage to
look at the bulletin board.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.000
Anne!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.280
Please, Jane. You must read the announcement.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.810
I'm going straight to the dressing room.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.550
When you've seen it, you must
come and tell me right away.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:45.490
But Anne, you'll miss the joy of
spotting your name on the board.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:46.610
That would be a pity.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.560
That doesn't matter.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.230
But if I've failed, don't console me first.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.360
Just tell me the result.
Don't bother about how I'll feel.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.840
You must promise me that much, Jane.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:04.100
All right, Anne. I promise you.
We're old friends after all.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.070
Thank you, Jane.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.770
Oh, I see!

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.420
Who? Who is it?

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.620
It's Gilbert Blythe!

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.750
The gold medal goes to Gilbert Blythe!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.100
That's great, Gilbert! Congratulations!

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.250
Thanks, Charlie.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.350
Congratulations, Gil!
I'm happy for you.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.820
Of course you'd be the
one to get the gold medal.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.890
Thanks, everybody. I'm really glad
to have won the gold medal of honor.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.820
To the winner of the gold medal: Hooray!

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.830
Gil... Gilbert got the medal.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.440
I was defeated by Gil...

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.960
Matthew will be so disappointed.
He was so sure I would win it.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.560
Hooray for Gilbert!

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.890
Hooray!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.140
Thank you!

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.360
Hooray!

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.830
It's Anne Shirley!
- Anne Shirley...

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.990
Hooray for Anne Shirley!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.730
Let's give three cheers to Anne Shirley,
winner of the Avery scholarship!

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.100
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.810
Congratulations, Anne!
It's great! I'm so happy for you.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.110
So I was right. You won
the Avery scholarship, after all.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.560
This is great, Anne!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.590
Congratulations, but it's a pity
you didn't win the gold medal.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.020
Thank you, Stella.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.050
Anne, you've done us proud.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.360
No, you've done the entire
Queen's Academy proud.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.780
Anne Shirley!

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:58.790
I didn't think you'd win the Avery,

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.310
but you've done very well!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.260
Josie...

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.080
And Gilbert has won the medal.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.420
I'm sure Miss Stacy and everyone in
Avonlea will be very pleased.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.580
Congratulations, Anne.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.920
Congratulations.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.100
Congratulations, Anne.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.840
Thank you, everyone. Thank you.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.840
Thank you so much!

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.820
I... I'm so happy.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:47.480
Matthew, I wonder what the results
of the announcement are for Anne.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:52.050
Well, now. I'm sure it will be a good result.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.610
She'll win the medal
and the scholarship...

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.770
Matthew, have you ever wondered

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.000
what will happen if Anne doesn't
get the scholarship?

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.050
Well, that...

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.970
Forget it. What will you do if Anne
doesn't get the scholarship?

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.040
What will I do...?

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.600
If that happens, she'll come
back here to be a teacher.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.050
Well, now...

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:17.890
No.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:24.200
Even if she doesn't get the scholarship,
I'll still send her to university.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.630
I'll find a way to raise the money.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.090
Besides, I have some savings.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.340
I knew you would say that.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:38.100
After all, she loves to study and
that's why her results are so good.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:42.120
Matthew, did you hear that Abbey Bank
has run into a financial crisis?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.130
I heard about it...

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.600
Should you be so carefree about it?

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.220
All our money is in Abbey Bank.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:57.520
If the bank closes down, we'll have
no money to send Anne to university.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.860
Don't worry, Marilla.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:05.530
Anne's likely to win the scholarship,
and Abbey Bank isn't in trouble.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.270
But it's better to check it.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.070
All right.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.480
Who could be here at this hour?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.550
Could it be Anne?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.370
It's the book supplier from Queen's Academy.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.620
As Anne's anxious to inform Matthew
and Marilla about her

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.180
having won the Avery scholarship,

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:34.030
she has asked the book supplier to
bring a letter on his way to Avonlea.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.090
Calm down, Matthew.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.570
Let me read it.
Aren't your eyes no good?

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:44.440
Never mind! I will read it.
Please sit down, Matthew.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.640
No, let me...

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.740
Dear Matthew and Marilla,

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:53.220
"I've passed the exams today.
Please don't worry."

00:09:54.450 --> 00:10:00.390
"And I was chosen as the
winner of the Avery scholarship."

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.350
A-Anne, really...

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.270
I always thought Anne would get it.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.930
She's really done well.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:18.140
"And Gilbert Blythe won the gold medal.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:22.110
"I intend to send him my
sincere congratulations.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:28.340
"The best thing is that
we can inform Miss Stacy

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.450
"that all her students have passed.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:36.830
"On this wonderful day, the future seems
to be filled with brightness.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.460
"I think I won't forget today
for the rest of my life.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:44.360
"This success has given
me a chance to change my fate.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.430
"It's a gift of love from the both of you.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:52.510
"To repay your love, I will strive to
study even harder from now on.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.810
"Thank you so much!

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.710
"My sincere thanks to both of you.

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.280
"From Anne, who can't wait
to hurry back to Green Gables."

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.010
Now you can stop worrying, Matthew.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.940
I wasn't worried at all.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.270
I'm going out for a while.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.090
Where are you going?

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:34.680
To Diana's place. I've got to tell
her the good news about Anne.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:38.900
You're going? You couldn't even
look her in the eye.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:43.880
Well, I'm sure Diana will want
to know as soon as possible.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:48.120
Well, you're not afraid of anything,
when it concerns Anne.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.970
But you can't go. The night air
is not good for your heart.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.290
But I can't really walk
outside during night time

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.450
with these eyes of mine, either.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.440
- I should-
- I know!

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.000
Matthew, there is a good way to do it!

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.690
Please watch. Now Diana
will come here in a hurry.

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:18.690
I see! That's Anne and Diana's signals!

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.750
Yes. Isn't it a great idea?

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:25.070
Now, then... Five times for 'Come right away', right?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.210
Five times. It means 'Come right away'.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.490
Anne's come back!

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.160
Diana, where are you going?!

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.790
It's Anne! Anne has come back!

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.390
Anne?

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.510
Anne!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:18.190
Anne isn't here, Diana.
I was the one who sent the signal.

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.100
I'm sorry to ask you
to come at this hour,

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.720
but we wanted to inform
you as soon as possible.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.150
Actually, Anne...

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.790
That's unfair, Matthew. I was speaking.

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.500
You know the results of the test?
Don't you?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.830
Yes, Anne...

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.200
...has won the Avery scholarship!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.970
Oh, Matthew!

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:42.540
The gold medal seems to
have been won by Gilbert Bryce.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.210
Oh! That's wonderful!

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:47.230
Really, really, really, really wonderful!

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.080
I'm so happy, it's like it happened to me!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.190
Anne! That's wonderful.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.320
You got the scholarship
you wanted to win the most!

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.250
Ah! I can't wait to see her!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:33.060
Before long, the day of the
graduation ceremony has arrived.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.900
The grand ceremony is held in the
large auditorium of Queen's Academy.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:42.540
Anne and all the others have worked so hard for this day.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.740
But at this moment, the hardship they've
gone through preparing for the exams,

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.610
feels like a thing of the distant past.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.510
Everyone goes through the ceremony
in a happy mood.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.890
The ceremony goes on smoothly.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.080
Following the speeches and the
congratulatory message,

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:02.390
the presentation of graduation certificates
and the conferment of the medal is carried out.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.860
But of all the attendees of the graduation ceremony,

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:13.940
the ones who look the proudest
are Matthew and Marilla.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:22.010
At this moment, their eyes and ears
are fixed on only one student on the stage.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.660
First Class certificate
awarded to Anne Shirley.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:32.090
During this year at Queen's Academy,
you have worked diligently

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:37.530
and studied National Language
and Literature with excellent results.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.320
To encourage your hard work,

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:45.270
the Avery Foundation will grant you
entrance to Redmond College,

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:51.210
and you'll also be provided with a scholarship
of $250 per year during your studies.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.720
She must be Anne Shirley.
What an outstanding child.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:10.520
Getting the Avery scholarship is really great, isn't it?

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.620
The graduation ceremony is
coming to an end.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:22.230
Dressed in her light green dress,
with faintly flushed cheeks,

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.590
and sparkling eyes,
Anne comes onto the stage.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:31.630
She recites the graduation essay
that has won her the Avery scholarship.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:37.530
Anne's voice echoes in every corner of the hall,

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:42.390
and touches everyone attending
the graduation ceremony.

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:56.630
Congratulations, Anne.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:57.800
Thank you, Ruby.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:03.910
Reckon you're glad we kept her, Marilla?

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:08.150
It's not the first time I've been glad.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.760
Aren't you proud of that Anne-girl?

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.620
Of course, I am, too.

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:20.220
After 70 years, I've finally found out that
there could be something so wonderful.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.430
How I wish to live even longer.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.300
After the graduation ceremony has ended,

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:31.900
Anne respectfully refuses Josephine Barry's
invitation to come to Beechwood,

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:36.140
and sets off for Avonlea
with the others in their carriage.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:41.980
Not having been home since April,
she cannot wait even one more day.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.100
Oh!

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:54.930
Matthew, could you please
stop for a while?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.880
I'm so relieved to be back here.

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.240
- Marilla.
- Yes?

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:24.410
When I crafted my dreams
and set out to realize them,

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:27.430
I didn't think it was anything serious
to leave my hometown.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:31.400
But sometimes I wanted so much to come
home and felt dreams didn't matter.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:35.130
I just wanted to hurry back home.
I wonder why.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.200
That's obvious, isn't it, Anne?

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.700
One's home town is a place like that.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:44.050
Avonlea is your hometown, Anne.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:51.550
Yes, Anne. No matter how far away you are,
you'll always be Anne of Avonlea,

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:54.060
and Anne of the Green Gables.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:56.860
In the past and in the days to come.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:57.930
Matthew...

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:02.220
Well, it's getting late. Let's go.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.500
Giddyup!

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:21.200
The light's still on in the house.

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:26.510
Who could it be?

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:29.550
Oh, it must be Martin, the hireling.

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:35.430
Anne! Anne!

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:37.260
My! Diana!

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.220
Diana!

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.470
Welcome back, Anne!

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:43.630
I'm back!

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.580
Did you come here to wait for me, Diana?

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.340
I was sure you would come back today.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.920
Oh, how I've wanted to see you, Diana.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:57.050
Me, too, Anne.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:00.830
Now, now. Go to your room
and have a good chat.

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.860
In the meantime, I will prepare tea.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:05.580
Yes! Thank you, Marilla.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.400
Diana, let's go!

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.270
Yes.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.770
What a fine relationship they have.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:22.720
Yes. I suppose they'll be
bosom friends forever.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.550
What a nice smell!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.740
What beautiful China roses.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:34.120
Marilla arranged them for me.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:39.850
Oh, how I've missed my room and the bay window!

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.970
Also, the pointed firs and the birches in the hollow.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.850
Oh, Diana! It feels so good to be home.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:52.030
The white orchard and the
Snow Queen are just like before.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:57.280
And what is more wonderful
than anything else is seeing you.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:02.320
Oh! I thought you would prefer that
classmate of yours, Stella Maynard.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:05.970
Josie Pye said you're infatuated with her.

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:12.800
Stella Maynard would be my favourite
if not for someone else,

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.960
and that someone is you.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.290
Our friendship is like this daffodil,
it won't wither easily.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:23.500
I'll just like you more and more.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.030
I'm relieved.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:27.810
I have so many things to tell you.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:33.110
But for now, sitting here and looking at you
is enough to make me happy.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.850
I guess I'm exhausted.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.750
Over the year,
I've been studying so hard,

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:42.230
and I wanted so much
to take the Avery scholarship,

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:43.920
that I didn't dare to relax at all.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.790
But you've done really well, Anne!

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:51.530
Now that you've got the Avery scholarship,
I suppose you won't want to be a teacher.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:56.640
That's right. For now, anyway.
I'll be going to Redmond in September.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:00.440
But I've heard that Redmond is a high level college.

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:01.960
I'm quite nervous about it.

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:04.370
You will be all right.

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.310
But that's in three months.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:10.210
And by the time the glorious, golden holiday is over,

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:13.270
I'll have a brand new stock of ambition laid in.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:17.150
It seems they have a lot to talk about.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:19.500
Well, they haven't seen
each other for a long time.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.950
Let's leave them alone for a while longer.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.560
All right.

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:30.580
When Anne leaves for Redmond,
we'll be lonely again.

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:34.990
Well, now. But that's three months from now.

00:22:35.780 --> 00:22:39.330
But it's for four years, and that's a long time.

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:45.150
Don't worry. She'll come home
once there's a break.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:46.290
That's true.

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:52.860
All of us plan to advance towards our ambitions.

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:55.020
Jane and Ruby want to become teachers.

00:22:55.070 --> 00:23:00.130
I heard the school in Newbridge has
extended an invitation to Jane.

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:03.030
I'm sure Jane will become a very good teacher.

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:06.080
I heard Gilbert's going to be a teacher, too.

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:07.020
What?

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:09.850
Isn't he going to Redmond?

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.990
It can't be helped.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:18.290
Gilbert's father can't afford to
send him to college next year,

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.790
so he seems to have no choice but to work.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:27.750
If Miss Ames resigns, Gilbert will
certainly teach at Avonlea school.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:34.620
When she hears that Gilbert
isn't going to college,

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:37.170
Anne feels a queer little sensation
of dismayed surprise.

00:23:38.010 --> 00:23:43.170
She had expected that Gilbert
would be going to Redmond also.

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:47.050
For so long, Anne has been motivating
herself by competing with Gilbert.

00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:49.680
Now that she has lost that rival,

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:52.630
will she be able to concentrate on her studies?

00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:55.430
That fear runs through her body,

00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:59.560
and feeling her dreams fading away rapidly,

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:03.400
Anne keeps sitting in her dark room.

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:22.480
Just as Anne realizes that Matthew
and Marilla are getting old,

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.940
Mrs. Lynde brings news that
makes her even more worried.

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:29.960
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 46

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.140
Matthew's Love

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:32.580
Please look forward to it!
